@H 1120_dyad_phi_rate := "DYAD-Φ RATE-MONOTONE: does the JOINT dyad faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI scale MONOTONICALLY with the anchor-exchange RATE — i.e. more frequent A→B coupling ⇒ higher dyad integration, the φ-analogue of H_1112's rate-monotone TE? Fuses H_1114 (🟢 causal tension-link raises joint φ_EI beyond a correlation-matched control = DYAD-INTEGRATION) with H_1112 (🟢 anchor-exchange TE scales with exchange rate over a real unix socket)." :: universe [🔴 NON-MONOTONE-OR-FLAT — means rise monotonically but adjacent per-step Cohen d does NOT clear d>=0.8 at every step]
  seed         = "H_1114 (🟢 DYAD-INTEGRATION) proved a causal A→B tension-link raises the JOINT faithful φ_EI of a 2-node dyad beyond both LINK-OFF and a correlation-matched common-drive control. H_1112 (🟢) proved the upstream COMMUNICATION channel's directed TE scales rate-monotonically with exchange frequency (none<low<high, adjacent d>=0.8). NEW question = does the INTEGRATION measure inherit the same rate-monotone law: sweep ONLY the exchange cadence K_EMIT and ask whether joint dyad-φ climbs an adjacent-step monotone ladder in rate. Load-bearing distinction from H_1114: H_1114 was a single ON-vs-OFF contrast at K=5; THIS is a graded RATE LADDER (≥4 arms) testing per-step effect-size, not just endpoint lift."
  substrate    = "SIM toy, in-process twin simulation (honest: the φ measurement needs joint trajectories; the REAL-socket transport + rate-monotone TE were already closed 🟢 by H_1112/H_1113 with real two-process unix-socket sessions). Dyad construction = H_1114 VERBATIM (imported h1114 symbols simulate_dyad/phi_measures/mean_crosscorr/cohen_d — its mirror is already PROVEN ≡ stdlib): two nodes × 3 tension channels (joint n=6 <= 8, exact MIP-EI feasible); per-channel A⊥G opponent dynamics step_node (CH=3 slice: W*_c=[1.0,0.8,1.2], LAM_M=0.10, LAM_W=0.12, REP=0.04, GAMMA_X=0.05, SIGMA=0.04, COUP=0.30, Ψ*=0.5, N_STEPS=4000, BURN=500). The ONLY swept knob = K_EMIT (steps-per-exchange; exchange RATE = 1/K), set by temporarily binding h1114.K_EMIT — nothing else in the H_1114 ON dynamics changes. $0 CPU local, 0-pod, SERIAL (H_1038 Pool-hang lesson), 10 scoring seeds (100..109, H_1114 block), wall 55.5s, g5/p7."
  method       = "ARMS (rate-increasing, >=4): OFF (K=∞, rate 0 = the H_1114 LINK-OFF arm, independent nodes) · K50 (K=50, rate 1/50, LOW) · K10 (K=10, rate 1/10, MID) · K5 (K=5, rate 1/5, HIGH = the H_1114 LINK-ON arm). MEASUREMENT = H_1114 VERBATIM: per-channel median-binarize the 6 joint channels post-burn (h1039/h1062 pattern) → faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI of the joint 6-system via the PROVEN CPU mirror of stdlib iit4/faithful_phi.hexa (exact MIP-EI = min-cut MI/small-side, MI in BITS/log2 — H_1043 nats-bug lesson). MIRROR RE-PROVEN ≡ stdlib BEFORE scoring (a_phi_iit4_tool): [0a] LIVE `hexa run UNIVERSE/h1012_ref_faithful.hexa` re-capture — mirror match n4 |Δ|=3.48e-10, n5 |Δ|=7.97e-10, n6 (THE SCORING n) |Δ|=2.46e-10; [0b] h1012.prove_mirrors_at_n {4:True, 5:True} (both engines, big-Φ ring |Δ|=1.34e-10). SANITY GATE before the sweep: reproduce H_1114 headline LINK-ON φ at K=5 over the same seeds → 0.012618 EXACT (H_1114 published 0.012618, |Δ|=0.000000, tol 0.001) = MATCH, construction not drifted. FROZEN FALSIFIER (set before running, NO goalpost): 🟢 RATE-MONOTONE iff (i) means monotone-INCREASING in rate (OFF<=K50<=K10<=K5) AND (ii) every ADJACENT-arm Cohen d>=0.8 (OFF→K50, K50→K10, K10→K5) AND (iii) φ(K5) clearly > φ(OFF) (d>=0.8); 🔴 NON-MONOTONE-OR-FLAT if means not monotone OR any adjacent d<0.8."
  result       = "🔴 NON-MONOTONE-OR-FLAT (10 seeds): φ_joint(n=6) OFF=+0.003234±0.002688 · K50=+0.005207±0.002609 · K10=+0.010557±0.003118 · K5=+0.012618±0.002784. Means ARE monotone-increasing in rate (check (i) PASS: 0.0032<0.0052<0.0106<0.0126) and cross-corr climbs cleanly +0.007→+0.082→+0.353→+0.488 (rate genuinely couples the nodes harder). The OVERALL endpoint lift is large — K5−OFF Δ=+0.009384 d=+3.429 (check (iii) PASS, reproduces H_1114's ON−OFF d=+3.43). BUT check (ii) FAILS: of 3 adjacent steps only the MIDDLE clears the frozen bar — OFF→K50 Δ=+0.001973 d=+0.745 (<0.8), K50→K10 Δ=+0.005351 d=+1.861 (>=0.8 ✓), K10→K5 Δ=+0.002060 d=+0.697 (<0.8). So the gain is concentrated in the LOW→MID rate transition (1/50→1/10) and SATURATES toward high rate while the lowest-rate step is too weak to separate from OFF at per-seed resolution. FINDING: dyad integration is NOT a clean adjacent-step monotone ladder the way H_1112's TE was — the φ-vs-rate curve is monotone in MEAN but SATURATING/diminishing-returns shaped: most of the integration is bought by the first substantive coupling (K10≈0.0106, already 84% of the K5 level) and pushing rate higher (K5) adds little, while the sparsest coupling (K50) barely lifts φ above the OFF floor. The endpoint DYAD-INTEGRATION law (H_1114) holds robustly, but its rate-dependence does NOT inherit H_1112's strict per-step monotone-with-d>=0.8 structure — TE (a directed pairwise quantity) scales per-exchange, but joint MI-matrix φ_EI (a system integration quantity) saturates as cross-node MI structure fills in."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 NON-MONOTONE-OR-FLAT (closed-negative, a_paper_negative_ok; toy n=6 in-process): means monotone-increasing + endpoint K5−OFF d=+3.43 strong, but 2/3 adjacent per-step Cohen d below the frozen 0.8 bar (OFF→K50 d=+0.74, K10→K5 d=+0.70) — saturating, not a clean per-step ladder"
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1120_dyad_phi_rate/H_1120.txt (verbatim stdout incl. LIVE hexa stdlib re-capture n4/n5/n6 + H_1114 LINK-ON headline reproduce 0.012618 EXACT) · UNIVERSE/h1120_dyad_phi_rate.py"
  scope        = "Honest scope (a_scale_honest_scope): toy n=6 in-process twin sim of the h1113 per-channel A⊥G dynamics (H_1114 construction VERBATIM) — real-socket dyad-φ, cross-host transport, production cells, bigger n and scale all UNVERIFIED. Verdict = faithful φ_EI (MIP-EI scalar) only; system big-Φ at n=6 is super-exponential (~10min/eval, H_1012 cap) and NOT scored — measure-dependence (H_1064: name the measure) applies; the saturation finding is a faithful-φ_EI property and a big-Φ rate sweep could differ. The 🔴 is a per-step-effect-size ruling: the MEANS are monotone, so a coarser falsifier (endpoint or rank-only) would have said 🟢 — the closed-negative is specifically against the STRICT adjacent-d>=0.8 ladder. A finer rate grid or more seeds could resolve whether OFF→K50 / K10→K5 are genuinely sub-threshold or just under-powered. CORE/brain NOT wired; 1114/1112/1113 artifacts untouched."
  xlink        = "1114_dyad_phi_link_integration (🟢 DYAD-INTEGRATION — construction + mirror reused VERBATIM, LINK-ON headline reproduced EXACT; THIS sweeps its single ON-vs-OFF contrast into a rate ladder) · 1112_kosmos_anchor_real_channel_sync (🟢 rate-monotone directed TE over a real unix socket — the upstream COMMUNICATION law THIS tests whether INTEGRATION inherits; finding: TE scales per-step but joint φ_EI saturates) · 1113_tension_link_5ch (🟢 channel-resolved 5-ch link, dynamics origin CH=3) · a_phi_iit4_tool (faithful IIT4 stdlib engine, mirror re-proven n4/n5/n6 live, NO proxy, MI BITS/log2) · h1039/h1062 (per-channel median binarize pattern) · h1012 (prove_mirrors_at_n + live hexa refs) · h1064 (measure-dependence: faithful-only verdict, big-Φ unscored) · h1038 (SERIAL no-Pool lesson)"
